n the highway.  [KERRY, Senator John EDWARDS&nbsp- campaign.] \n (Studio: John Seigenthaler)  Further coverage of the campaign on \"Meet the Press\" noted.", "segment_duration": 390, "segment_type_id": 2, "segment_start_time": "63050.0", "legacy_segment_id": 761200, "network_name": "NBC", "broadcast_type_name": "Evening News", "segment_type_name": "News", "segment_contributors_with_roles": null, "broadcast_contributors_with_roles": null, "topic_names": null, "location_names": null}, {"broadcast_id": "vy0ML9XO3t", "broadcast_date": "2004-07-31", "broadcast_start_time": "63000.0", "network": 3, "distributor": 10, "broadcast_title": "NBC Nightly News", "broadcast_type_id": 1, "broadcast_duration": 1720, "broadcast_description": null, "legacy_broadcast_id": 761199, "segment_id": "jlgFo0oH3j", "segment_broadcast_id": "vy0ML9XO3t", "segment_title": "September 11 / Commission Report", "segment_description": "(Studio: John Seigenthaler)  Report introduced.   (White House: Rosiland Jordan)  The question of the response from Congress & President Bush to the recommendations from the commission that investigated September 11 featured; details given about the suggestion to put a national intelligence director in the White House.  [Commission chair Thomas KEAN&#134;- comments on terrorist attacks.]  [9/11 victim's relatives Stephen PUSH&#134;, Rosemary DILLARD&#134;- comment on action.]  [NBC News analyst Juliette KAYYEM&#134;- compares this commission to other blue-ribbon investigations & the role of the victims' families.]  [NBC terrorism analyst Roger CRESSEY&#134;- wants the report's implementation thought out first.]", "segment_duration": 130, "segment_type_id": 2, "segment_start_time": "63440.0", "legacy_segment_id": 761201, "network_name": "NBC", "broadcast_type_name": "Evening News", "segment_type_name": "News", "segment_contributors_with_roles": null, "broadcast_contributors_with_roles": null, "topic_names": null, "location_names": null}, {"broadcast_id": "vy0ML9XO3t", "broadcast_date": "2004-07-31", "broadcast_start_time": "63000.0", "network": 3, "distributor": 10, "broadcast_title": "NBC Nightly News", "broadcast_type_id": 1, "broadcast_duration": 1720, "broadcast_description": null, "legacy_broadcast_id": 761199, "segment_id": "QPKAEq35We", "segment_broadcast_id": "vy0ML9XO3t", "segment_title": "Iraq / Kidnappings/Hostages / Muslim Nations' Role", "segment_description": "(Studio: John Seigenthaler)  The kidnapping of two Turkish truck drivers in Iraq reported.   (Baghdad: James Hattori)  The surge of kidnappings by insurgents in Iraq of foreigners, including many Muslims, & the issue of help in Iraq from Muslim nations featured; videos shown of hostages; map shown of regional countries offering help.  [Secretary of State Colin POWELL&nbsp- comments on the proposal by Saudi Arabia of Arab troops in Iraq.]  [NBC military analyst retired Lt. Col. Rick FRANCONA&#134;- says the Muslim countries are more willing to participate.]  [Arab League envoy Ali HAMID&#134;- says the problem is the occupation of Iraq.]", "segment_duration": 140, "segment_type_id": 2, "segment_start_time": "63570.0", "legacy_segment_id": 761202, "network_name": "NBC", "broadcast_type_name": "Evening News", "segment_type_name": "News", "segment_contributors_with_roles": null, "broadcast_contributors_with_roles": null, "topic_names": null, "location_names": null}, {"broadcast_id": "vy0ML9XO3t", "broadcast_date": "2004-07-31", "broadcast_start_time": "63000.0", "network": 3, "distributor": 10, "broadcast_title": "NBC Nightly News", "broadcast_type_id": 1, "broadcast_duration": 1720, "broadcast_description": null, "legacy_broadcast_id": 761199, "segment_id": "NhdIV3P3tI", "segment_broadcast_id": "vy0ML9XO3t", "segment_title": "Upcoming Items (Studio: John Seigenthaler)", "segment_description": "null", "segment_duration": 20, "segment_type_id": 2, "segment_start_time": "63710.0", "legacy_segment_id": 761203, "network_name": "NBC", "broadcast_type_name": "Evening News", "segment_type_name": "News", "segment_contributors_with_roles": null, "broadcast_contributors_with_roles": null, "topic_names": null, "location_names": null}, {"broadcast_id": "vy0ML9XO3t", "broadcast_date": "2004-07-31", "broadcast_start_time": "63000.0", "network": 3, "distributor": 10, "broadcast_title": "NBC Nightly News", "broadcast_type_id": 1, "broadcast_duration": 1720, "broadcast_description": null, "legacy_broadcast_id": 761199, "segment_id": "Lggmchj6X6", "segment_broadcast_id": "vy0ML9XO3t", "segment_title": "(Commercial: Allegra; Prevacid; Oral-B; Cialis; Thompson's Water Seal; Metamucil.)", "segment_description": "null", "segment_duration": 150, "segment_type_id": 3, "segment_start_time": "63730.0", "legacy_segment_id": 761204, "network_name": "NBC", "broadcast_type_name": "Evening News", "segment_type_name": "Commercial", "segment_contributors_with_roles": null, "broadcast_contributors_with_roles": null, "topic_names": null, "location_names": null}, {"broadcast_id": "vy0ML9XO3t", "broadcast_date": "2004-07-31", "broadcast_start_time": "63000.0", "network": 3, "distributor": 10, "broadcast_title": "NBC Nightly News", "broadcast_type_id": 1, "broadcast_duration": 1720, "broadcast_description": null, "legacy_broadcast_id": 761199, "segment_id": "TdG95T33d3", "segment_broadcast_id": "vy0ML9XO3t", "segment_title": "In Depth (Hurricane Season)", "segment_description": "(Studio: John Seigenthaler)  Weather map shown of the first tropical storm of the season. \n (Miami: Kerry Sanders)  The soaring cost of hurricane insurance examined; scenes shown of the damages from costly Hurricane Andrew in 1992.  [Galveston, Texas, Katie HART; Floridians Nancy McHUGH&nbsp- comment on the cost of insurance.]  [Miami-Dade County commissioner Sally HEYMAN&#134;- says don't put the cost on the backs of homeowners.]  [Insurance Information Inst. Robert HARTWIG&#134;- says they are paying for the NEXT Andrew.]", "segment_duration": 150, "segment_type_id": 2, "segment_start_